+# Due date for todos — Implementation Plan
+
+> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (recommended) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan task-by-task. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.
+
+**Goal:** Todos get an optional, date-only due date; a todo is overdue when it is not done and its due date is before today (UTC). Overdue is visible in the JSON API (computed `overdue` flag, `GET /todos?overdue=` filter) and on the list page („überfällig" marker plus a "nur überfällige" toggle). Ticket #1.
+
+**Architecture:** `Todo` gains `DateOnly? DueDate` and a computed `Overdue` property — one rule shared by the API and the page. `TodoPatch` carries the due date as a tri-state (`DueDatePatch` + a System.Text.Json converter) so an explicit JSON `null` clears it while an absent field keeps it. `TodoStore.List(bool? overdue = null)` does the filtering; `GET /todos?overdue=...` and the page toggle both call it. The page stays read-only for todo data (no input for the date).
+
+**Tech Stack:** .NET 10, Blazor Web App (Interactive Server render mode), minimal APIs, System.Text.Json, xUnit + `WebApplicationFactory<Program>`.
+
+**Spec:** `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-01-due-date-design.md` (posted as Approved Spec on ticket #1)
+
+## Global Constraints
+
+- No new NuGet packages.
+- Validation errors stay `System.ComponentModel.DataAnnotations.ValidationException`, mapped to HTTP 400 `{"error": "..."}` by the existing middleware in `Program.cs`. Malformed bodies and invalid due dates throw `JsonException` → `BadHttpRequestException` → the same 400 shape (the converter must let the `JsonException` propagate).
+- TDD: failing test first, then minimal implementation, then a green test run, then commit.
+- Every UI element tests rely on carries a `data-testid`.
+- JSON is camelCase; todo response property order is `id, title, done, dueDate, overdue`.
+- End-to-end: the agent starts the app on http://localhost:3000 and drives it with Playwright; screenshots go outside the repo (e.g. under `/tmp/opencode`).
+
+## Review Focus
+
+1. Invalid due dates (`"2026-02-30"`, `"30.02.2026"`, `"next Friday"`) must yield 400, not 500 → API tests in Task 2.
+2. PATCH `{"dueDate": null}` must clear the date while an omitted field must keep it — a tri-state mix-up silently wipes or keeps dates → store tests in Task 1 plus an API test in Task 2.
+3. Boundary: due today (UTC) is NOT overdue; a done todo is never overdue; no date → never overdue → store test in Task 1.
+4. `GET /todos?overdue=banana` must yield 400 → API test in Task 2.
+5. The prerendered page HTML already contains the new `data-testid`s; the "nur überfällige" toggle filters once the Blazor circuit connects → page test in Task 3 plus E2E in Task 4.
+
+---
